sycl: nvfp4 in the ESIMD grouped GEMM

HomeBrain patch on ggml-sycl. Applies on top of 0013.
Upstream tracking: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/32757

Inkling's NVFP4 MoE experts took the joint_matrix grouped GEMM, which stages
each dequantized A tile through SLM, while q8_0 and the K-quants have an ESIMD
kernel that decodes straight into the dpas operand. This adds NVFP4 to it. A
32-value k step is two 16-value sub-blocks, one per k half, each with one
UE4M3 scale; the e2m1 codes come from the iq4 pair table in SLM, loaded with
the e2m1 codebook. Every code times a scale is exact in half, so one half
multiply rounds as the joint_matrix stage does. On the Arc Pro B60, 128
experts top-8 at 512 tokens: gate_up [2304x2304] 5537 -> 3421 us, down
[1152 -> 2304] 2938 -> 1704 us.

